B.aXM=new A.kr(B.zL,"Open their profile before you accept","Tap any mechanic's card on your bids list to see their profile. It shows their reviews, experience, certifications and more. It only takes a minute and nothing is charged by looking.")
B.aXF=new A.kr(B.iB,"Read the reviews, not just the stars","The star rating is a quick summary, but the written comments tell you what the work was actually like: was the mechanic on time, clear about the price, and easy to deal with? A mechanic with a few great reviews can be a better pick than one with a single five-star rating.")
B.a0G=new A.aw(61525,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.aXK=new A.kr(B.a0G,'"No reviews yet" just means new',"Everyone starts with zero reviews. If a mechanic is new, look at the rest of their profile, such as experience and certifications, and decide how comfortable you feel.")
B.aXL=new A.kr(B.rQ,"Check certifications that match your problem","ASE certifications show a mechanic passed tests in a specific area, like brakes or electrical. Their profile lists which ones they hold. A certification in the area of your problem is a good sign, but it is one sign among several, not the whole picture.")
B.aXC=new A.kr(B.hj,"Look for the insurance line",'If a mechanic has insurance paperwork on file, their profile says "insured until" a date. YCYC looks over the paperwork but does not verify coverage with the insurer, so if it matters to you, ask the mechanic directly.')
B.aXG=new A.kr(B.ke,"Notice the blue check","A blue check next to a name means YCYC has verified that mechanic's account. It is a good starting point, and it works best together with reviews and experience.")
B.aXD=new A.kr(B.zT,"Experience, warranty, and how they work","Years of experience, whether they offer a warranty, and whether they come to you (mobile) or work from a shop are all shown on the profile. Pick what fits your situation. For example, you may care most about a warranty on a bigger repair.")
B.aXI=new A.kr(B.n5,"Compare the whole bid, not only the price","The lowest price is not always the best fit, and the highest is not always better. Look at the price together with the arrival time, the reviews and the profile. If one bid is very different from the others, open that profile and see why it might be. On a diagnostic, each bid shows hours and an hourly rate, and the total is the final price.")
B.zM=new A.aw(62265,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.aXJ=new A.kr(B.zM,"Pick a time that works for you","Each bid shows when the mechanic can arrive. A good price does not help if the time does not work for you.")
B.aXH=new A.kr(B.hg,"Keep everything in the app","When you tap Accept, you pay through YCYC. Your card is held, not charged, until the work is done and you confirm it. Paying outside the app gives up that protection.")
B.zA=new A.aw(57948,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.aXE=new A.kr(B.zA,"There is no rush, and it is your choice","You do not have to accept the first bid. Take a moment, compare, and go with the mechanic you feel best about.")
